q:
From the hoeing and the mowing and the lavender rows gray;
 From laying down the runners down to Warsash way;
 Kerchieved as the buttercup,
 Ringèd as the moon,
 Beaded like the briony, scarlet-threaded soon;
 Driving in the tilted cart from smoky tent and tan,
 Rumbling down the roadway in the red caravan!
